    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0261" n="145" xml:id="pg145"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/978.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American
                    Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-02T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 2, 1912—12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your July 1.</p>
                <p>The Department concurs with the British Government in its view that loans to
                    China should not be made without adequate provisions for supervision of
                    expenditures. You may join your colleagues in representations to that effect. By
                    “adequate provisions for supervision” the Department has in mind substantially
                    the bases of the bankers’ telegram of May 15 without insistence upon the
                    financial agency.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
